      "nsfwLevel": 3,
      "description": "<p><strong><u>v1.5.4</u>: </strong>Fixed <strong>force_audio</strong> not actually working.  Fixed optional match image input being disconnected in &lt;Picture 2&gt;.</p><p><strong><u>v1.5.3</u>: </strong>Reverted the chain sampling implementation from 1.5.2. Currently too experimental.</p><p><strong><u>v1.5.2</u>:</strong></p><ul><li><p>D'ya know the expression, \"you have to break a few eggs to make an omelet\"? This fixes an issue where the \"Second Pass\" toggle had an inverted effect <code>Disabled = Yes / Enabled = No</code>. <strong>FIXED</strong></p></li><li><p>Added improved chain sampling logic, so you can optionally return leftover noise from a not fully denoised First Pass.</p></li></ul><p><strong><u>v1.5.1</u>: </strong>Fix error when not using video inputs. Sorry to any who snatched v1.5 right away and experienced this.</p><p><strong><u>v1.5</u>:</strong></p><p><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://github.com/altoiddealer/comfyui_essential-er\"><strong>ComfyUI-essential-er</strong></a> (my repo) is now <strong>required.</strong></p><p><strong>Reason: </strong>Extremely useful video/audio merging node which <strong><u>KJNodes has failed to merge</u></strong> from both <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://github.com/kijai/ComfyUI-KJNodes/pull/699\"><strong>a PR I had opened</strong></a>, as well as another user's <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://github.com/kijai/ComfyUI-KJNodes/pull/691\"><strong>still open PR</strong></a>.</p><p>In terms of this workflow, it turns <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/vOTuBqV.png\"><strong>this</strong></a> (v1.4) into <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"ugc\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/sne4CXI.png\"><strong>this</strong></a> (v1.5).</p><p><strong><u>New Feature:</u></strong></p><p>\"Seamless Continuation\" has been replaced with \"Seamless Extension\"</p><p><u>Seamless Extension modes:</u></p><ul><li><p><strong>Seamless Continuation</strong> (generate from your video onwards)</p></li><li><p><strong>Seamless Convergence</strong> (generate into your source video)</p></li><li><p><strong>Can be used in combination</strong></p></li></ul>",
